# Parent chain Deliver (Falryn maintainer)

Applies when the prompt is `Deliver — Target: Parent chain #…` or `/loop` with that Deliver target in **tyldra-org/falryn**.

Load **`falryn/.agents/skills/falryn-loop/SKILL.md`** first. It wins over global background-CI defaults.

## Standing authorization (this run)

Without asking:

- commit, push, branch, open and **squash-merge** PRs (docs companion first, then falryn)
- update GitHub Project status and assignees
- foreground `gh run watch` until required checks pass or fail

## Do not stop mid-chain

While native children of the parent remain incomplete:

- do not end the turn after merge, CI start, or a status report
- do not defer with “continuing next step” or “unless you want to pause”
- do not emit `Deliver — Target: Issue #<sibling>` (Parent-issue handoff)

After each child: reconcile GitHub, then **immediately** start the next sibling.

## CI

**Foreground** wait during Deliver — not background. Background is only when the host cuts the turn; user resumes via `/loop` with the same Parent chain target.

## When you may stop

- explicit product or contract question (`awaiting-input`)
- failed merge preconditions
- three CI repair attempts without progress

Only then emit `Suggested next prompt: Deliver — Target: Parent chain #<parent>` for resume.
